  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Equity &amp; inclusion - equal education opportunities for vulnerable populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Nations (UN) 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development pledges to leave no one behind. The agenda promises a &#x2018;just, equitable, tolerant, open and socially inclusive world in which the needs of the most disadvantaged are met&#x2019;. However, disadvantage factors associated with gender, disability, location, wealth, migration status and ethnicity hinder the achievement of equal, quality and inclusive education opportunities for all. UNESCO Montevideo will support Member States with their development of rights-based, inclusive and equitable education systems with focus on those at greatest risk of being left behind. The above will be achieved by supporting MS with their monitoring, adherence and implementation of human rights instruments, knowledge- generation, knowledge-sharing and advocacy activities at country and cross-country levels.</narrative>
  </description>
